config BR2_PACKAGE_SIGMASTAR_BOOT
	bool "sigmastar-boot"
	depends on BR2_TARGET_UBOOT
	help
	  Board hooks for Buildroot's U-Boot package on SigmaStar.

	  U-Boot builds u-boot.bin; a SigmaStar board boots a container --
	  IPL, GCIS, IPL_CUST, SNI and the compressed payload -- which the
	  vendor's make_boot_spinor.sh assembles. This runs it, checks that
	  it produced something (nothing in that chain sets -e, and a
	  container with no payload writes cleanly and never boots), and
	  installs the result as images/u-boot-<soc>-nor.bin.

	  It also carries the version string the board reports, the SoC
	  macro the vendor tree expects as a compiler flag, and the rsync
	  exclusions that make UBOOT_SRCDIR builds repeatable.

	  Not part of the sysupgrade tarball: mtd0 has no software recovery
	  path, so writing it is a deliberate act with a programmer to hand.
	  `make fullimage` picks it up.
